                    {
                        "sense_id": "98b88557-c46e-368b-977d-e8c5c8c55eff",
                        "entry_id": "2cafd15e-7542-390a-8a01-f8c1fb5ea49d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A female given name from the Germanic languages, a latinized form of Louise used since the eighteenth century."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5268a9d-d52f-49b6-bba0-c912d2d579cf",
                                "sense_id": "98b88557-c46e-368b-977d-e8c5c8c55eff",
                                "text": "But certainly there are some names which seem to belong to particular classes of character, to form the mind and even influence the destiny: Louisa, now; - is not your Louisa necessarily a die-away damsel, who reads novels, and holds her head on one side, languishing and given to love!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd3a2c9e-e21c-468c-a09e-c2e1f265e133",
                                "sense_id": "98b88557-c46e-368b-977d-e8c5c8c55eff",
                                "text": "On being told that Mrs. Bounderby was there, she replied, at cross-purposes, that she had never called him by that name since he married Louisa; that pending her choice of an objectionable name, she had called him J; and that she could not at present depart from that regulation, not being yet provided with a permanent substitute."
                            }
                        ]
